            "abstract": "<title>Abstract</title>\n                <p>The O(N²) cost of self-attention is structural: N tokens require O(N²) computation and an O(N) cache  that grows with context. This work eliminates the cost: attention is computed between the current  token and a single persistent vector—the ocean state, the previous hidden state—so each step costs  O(1) in computation and memory. Only two repositionings to a standard Transformer: the ocean state,  and BPTT for the backward pass. The ocean state outperforms the standard Transformer, with a stable  training gain without exception, and at 10 million steps of context it shows no sign of forgetting.</p>",
